                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "what if parsed object is empty ?\n\nthe user first need to check ConfigManager object is exists and later has to check system config json is not empty.\nif parsed json object is empty, better not allow configManager object creation ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/config_manager.hpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "If parsed object is empty, `buildConfigMaps()` throws an exception which will propagate to the caller, in this case `Manager` who can handle it. This is inline with our \"validate JSON at single place\" roadmap."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/config_manager.hpp",
